course: dictionary
lesson: 3608
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The word figure is a good example. To know which meaning is right, look at the words around it, which is its context. Ask yourself: what kind of thing is being talked about?
explain: «Only a tiny share of boys who join a football academy young become professionals; the figure often quoted is under 1 in 100.» Here we are talking about chances, so figure means a number. In maths, a figure can be a flat shape, like a triangle. A figure can also be a person, or a small toy model of a person.
explain: Figure also appears in the phrase figure out, which means to find the answer or to understand. «Can you figure out how many biscuits we need?» Here you have to work something out. When you meet figure, check the context first, then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: A figure can be a number written as a sign, like 7 or 25.
fact: A figure can be a flat shape, like a triangle or a square.
fact: A figure can be the shape of a person, or a small toy model of a person, such as an action figure.
fact: To figure out something is to find the answer or to understand it.
fact: Figure is a noun and a verb: figures, figured and figuring are all forms of the word.
exercise: «Only a tiny share of boys who join a football academy young become professionals; the figure often quoted is under 1 in 100.» What does figure mean here? | A person standing still | *A number, written with digits | A drawing in a book | A triangle with three sides
exercise: «Toad is a short, stout figure, splashing badly and rolling a good deal.» What does figure mean here? | *The shape of a person | A number | To find an answer | A diagram in a science book
exercise: Mia asks, «Can you figure out how many biscuits we need?» What does figure out mean? | To count the biscuits in the tin | To throw the biscuits away | To draw a picture of biscuits | *To find the answer
test: In «the figure hears a scream passing through nature and covers its ears», what does figure mean? | To find the answer | A number | A flat shape like a square | *A person or shape in the picture
test: Which phrase means to find the answer? | In figures | Action figure | *Figure out | See Figure 2
exam: In maths, what is a plane figure? | A number written as a sign | *A flat shape, like a square | A word that means to find the answer | A toy model of a person
